# Define the portable `dist/` layout and `game/manifest/dist.json`

Define one machine-readable product contract for the final per-platform package
without freezing incidental Unreal DLL inventories. The manifest describes
entrypoints, required runtime roots, mod directory, launcher helpers, package
kind, and integrity expectations for each target.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Add tracked `game/manifest/dist.json` with a versioned schema covering all
  supported target identities and their required layout invariants.
- [ ] Model Windows/Linux/macOS as portable game directories, Android as APK,
  and iOS as unsigned/local-sideload IPA output.
- [ ] Require a `mods/` directory in portable runtime layouts where the platform
  supports external mod placement.
- [ ] Do not imitate Fortnite launcher/EAC/Epic metadata (`.egstore`, Cloud,
  launcher, anti-cheat) unless SHAR independently acquires a real requirement.
- [ ] Avoid hardcoding every Engine/runtime DLL name; validate semantic roots,
  native entrypoints, packaged content, notices, and platform-native runtime
  dependencies instead.
- [ ] Update README examples whenever the versioned dist contract changes.

## Dependencies

Depends on final package evidence from the canonical multi-platform runner.

## Evidence

The Windows package already proves the useful Unreal shape is a small portable
runtime, not a Fortnite-sized launcher installation.
